{{/* @dot github.com/donseba/go-partial/examples/docs.DocsPage */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400 text-[13px] font-extrabold uppercase text-emerald-300">Reference</p>
    <h1 class="max-w-4xl text-5xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-slate-50">Connectors</h1>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">Connectors let go-partial understand request headers from a frontend library or a custom fetch client.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Choose a connector</h2>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root := partial.New("shell.gohtml").SetConnector(connector.NewHTMX4(nil)).SetFileSystem(os.DirFS("web"))</code></pre>

    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The connector is applied to wrapper partials, content partials, registered regions, selected partials, and out-of-band partials rendered through the root.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Included connectors</h2>
    <table class="w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-800/90 text-left">
        <thead class="bg-slate-900"><tr><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Connector</th><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Target header</th><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Use</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.NewPartial</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">X-Target</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Framework-neutral requests from fetch, tests, or custom clients.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.NewHTMX4</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Target</code> (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">tagName#id</code>)</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">htmx 4 requests, boosted navigation, response headers, and OOB updates. This site uses it.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.NewHTMX</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Target</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">The same for htmx 2.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.NewUnpoly</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">X-Up-Target</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Unpoly fragment requests.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.NewTurbo</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Turbo-Frame</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Turbo Frame requests.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Alpine, Stimulus, Vue, and similar frontend libraries do not need built-in connectors unless they define a stable fragment-request protocol. Use <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.NewPartial</code> or a custom connector when your own fetch layer sends project-specific headers.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Shared connector values</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Every connector exposes the same concepts to go-partial:</p>
    <table class="w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-800/90 text-left">
        <thead class="bg-slate-900"><tr><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Concept</th><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Generic header</th><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Template helper</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Target</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">X-Target</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ targetValue }}" }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Selection</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">X-Select</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ selectionValue }}" }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Action</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">X-Action</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ actionValue }}" }}</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Framework-specific connectors may use a different target header, such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Target</code> or <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">X-Up-Target</code>. Selection and action headers stay generic unless the connector defines otherwise.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">URL query fallback</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Set <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">UseURLQuery</code> when a client cannot send custom headers. go-partial will read <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">target</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">select</code>, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">action</code> from the query string after checking headers.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root := partial.New("shell.gohtml").
    SetConnector(connector.NewPartial(&connector.Config{
        UseURLQuery: true,
    }))</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Response instructions</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Partials can set protocol-neutral response instructions. The connector turns them into response headers when supported.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">content.Response().
    Retarget("#notice").
    ReswapWith(connector.NewSwap().Style(connector.SwapOuterHTML)).
    TriggerWith(connector.NewTrigger().AddEvent("saved"))</code></pre>

    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">With the HTMX connector, this writes headers such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Retarget</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Reswap</code>, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Trigger</code>.</p>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The response builder, trigger builder, and swap builder are mutable convenience values. Build them during route setup or inside one request, then attach the finished response. Do not keep mutating the same builder from multiple goroutines.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Custom connector</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">If your frontend sends different headers, implement the connector interface in your application.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">type Connector interface {
    RenderPartial(r *http.Request) bool
    GetTargetValue(r *http.Request) string
    GetSelectValue(r *http.Request) string
    GetActionValue(r *http.Request) string

    GetTargetHeader() string
    GetSelectHeader() string
    GetActionHeader() string
    ResponseHeaders(response connector.Response) map[string]string
}</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">External references</h2>
    <ul class="grid list-disc gap-2 pl-6 text-slate-400">
        <li><a href="https://htmx.org/reference/">HTMX reference</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://turbo.hotwired.dev/handbook/frames">Turbo Frames handbook</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://unpoly.com/X-Up-Target">Unpoly X-Up-Target</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Related integration docs</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">For practical usage, see the <a href="/docs/integrations" hx-get="/docs/integrations" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">integration overview</a>, <a href="/docs/integrations/htmx" hx-get="/docs/integrations/htmx" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">HTMX integration</a>, and <a href="/docs/integrations/sse" hx-get="/docs/integrations/sse" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">SSE integration</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Asking about a request</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Handlers ask the connector instead of reading protocol headers. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">IsRequest</code> is also true for an htmx 4 request for the whole page, which <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">RenderPartial</code> is not.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">conn := root.Connector()

connector.IsRequest(conn, r)
connector.IsBoosted(conn, r)
connector.CurrentURL(conn, r)
connector.VaryHeaders(conn)</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Redirects</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.Redirect</code> answers a request, such as a posted form, by sending the client on: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Location</code> with status 200 for a request htmx made, a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">303 See Other</code> otherwise, which browsers, Turbo and Unpoly follow.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">connector.Redirect(root.Connector(), w, r, connector.Location{Path: "/orders", Target: "#content"})</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Neutral attributes</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.Attrs(conn, connector.Attr{Confirm: "Delete?", Boost: connector.BoostOff, Target: "#list"})</code> returns the attributes in the connector's syntax, such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-confirm</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-boost</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">up-confirm</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">up-follow</code>, or <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-turbo-confirm</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-turbo</code>.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Requests for tests</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.SetRequestTarget(conn, req, "comments")</code> makes a request ask for a target as the client library would, the inverse of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">GetTargetValue</code>.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Page settings and submit buttons</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.Attr</code> also writes the settings of a whole page: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Inherit</code> gives them to the descendants (htmx 4's <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">:inherited</code>), <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">DisableWhileRequest</code> names the elements disabled during a request, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">KeepOnServerError</code> leaves the page as it is on a 5xx response. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SubmitConfirm</code> asks a question before a submit button sends its form: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-turbo-confirm</code> with Turbo, else <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-partial-confirm</code>, asked by the client of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/interactions</code>. Templates write them with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clientAttrs</code>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;body {{ "{{ clientAttrs runtime \"inherit\" \"true\" \"boost\" \"on\" \"target\" \"#content\" \"swap\" \"outerHTML\" \"disableWhileRequest\" \"find button[type='submit']\" \"keepOnServerError\" \"true\" }}" }}&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.MergeAttrs(conn, attrs, attr, kinds...)</code> replaces the connector's attributes of a setting in a map of attributes another library built; <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.Apply(conn, w.Header(), connector.Response{PushURL: "false"})</code> sets response headers in one call; <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.OOBAttrs(conn, "beforeend")</code>, or <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ oobSwap \"beforeend\" }}" }}</code> in templates, writes the out-of-band attribute.</p>
</article>
